on 7.4x, UR supported only SSHv2. Starting from firmware Version 7.4x, UR added support to SSHv1. SSHv1 has known vulnerabilities (SSH protocol session key retrieval and insertion attack). SSH 1.2.25, 1.2.23, and other versions, when used in in CBC (Cipher Block Chaining) or CFB (Cipher Feedback 64 bits) modes, allows remote attackers to insert arbitrary data into an existing stream between an SSH client and server by using a known plaintext attack and computing a valid CRC-32 checksum for the packet, aka the \"SSH insertion attack.\"","text_sha256":"00d0f1cd28fab3c0d49814e3d07323b2c9aa6bdfb1d45b3c21c71a01f8c17a14","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/ics-advisories/icsa-21-075-02","document_sha256":"7a316b4711bda60a2925bfcddd87cf69b0759c96d9a81015e56e01a644d50e30","pointer":"/vulnerabilities/2/notes/0/text","product_keys":["icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0001","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0002","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0003","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0004","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0005","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0006","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0007","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0008","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0009","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0010","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0011","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0012","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0013","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0014","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0015","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0016","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0017","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0018","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0019"],"scope_binding":"CVE_known_affected_product_set_candidate_not_universal_condition","subject_ambiguous":false},{"id":"icsa-21-075-02:v2:n1","text":"SSVCv2/E:N/A:Y/2026-04-15T06:00:00.000000Z","text_sha256":"d4ebabe83b4ef82745e4e2447c5d0dd59baf6adb4bc4fe8ea01596aadbf4c555","url":"https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/ics-advisories/icsa-21-075-02","document_sha256":"7a316b4711bda60a2925bfcddd87cf69b0759c96d9a81015e56e01a644d50e30","pointer":"/vulnerabilities/2/notes/1/text","product_keys":["icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0001","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0002","icsa-21-075-02:CSAFPID-0003","icsa-21-075